            <div xml:id="d662">

                <pb facs="0703" n="585" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg585"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">312.1722 Sandino/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hawks</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-24T09:00:00-06:00">April 24, 1929—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>52. Referring to the Legation’s telegram of April 15, noon.<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d662-f1"/> The Minister for Foreign Affairs informed me last night
                    that yesterday the Mexican Ambassador had requested permission for Sandino to
                    pass through Guatemala from Salvador to Mexico; that this permission was granted
                    and that Sandino will be escorted through Guatemala, precautions being taken to
                    prevent any demonstration whatever.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nicaragua, Honduras and Salvador.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hawks</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
